{
                        "step": "Adjust pH of the medium to 7.1. Add 1.5% agar if needed. Autoclave for 15 min at 121\u00b0C. After sterilization add 25 ml each of filter-sterilized 20% glucose and 20% Na-malate."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Aseptically add one or more sterile strips of filter paper to slants or plates. Inoculate the filter papers with a small (5 mm x 5mm) agar cube or a piece of filter paper overgrown with the strain."
                    }

{
                        "step": "After sterilization, aseptically add 1 ml/l of a 10% solution of acetylacetone in ethanol."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Medium should be filled up into crew capped tubes (Wheaton)."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Add 4 ml Resazurin solution (25 mg/100 ml). 0.05% Cysteine-hydrochloride is added after the medium has been boiled and cooled and CO2. Distribute under N2 and autoclave."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Adjust pH to 7.0. For Bacillus strains the addition of 10.0 mg MnSO4 x H2O is recommended for sporulation."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Adjust pH to 7.4. After sterilization add 100 ml of a filter-sterilized solution of 1 mM diethyl phosphonate (Eastman Organic Chemical Div., Rochester, N.Y., USA) or of 20 mM phosphate buffer."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Sterilize medium and cool to about 45\u00b0C . Aseptically add 5% defibrinated blood."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Dissolve ingredients and adjust pH to 7.5. Sparge medium with 100% N2 gas for 30 - 45 min to make it anoxic. Distribute medium under same gas atmosphere in anoxic Hungate-type tubes or serum vials and autoclave."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Adjust pH to 7.0. Soil extract is prepared by sieving air dried garden soil through a coarse sieve and autoclaving 400 g with 960 ml of distilled water at 121\u00b0C for one hour. After the mixture is cool and settled, the supernatant is carefully decanted, filtered through paper, autoclaved in 200 ml quantities, and stored at room temperature until cleared by sedimentation."
                    }

{
                        "step": "After sterilization add 60 ml ethanol (50% v/v), sterilized by filtration."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Dissolve ingredients except cysteine and cellobiose and adjust pH to 7.2. Sparge medium with 100% N2 gas for 30 - 45 min to make it anoxic, then add cysteine and readjust pH to 7.2, if necessary. Dispense medium under the same gas atmosphere into anoxic Hungate-type tubes or serum vials and autoclave. Prior to inoculation add cellobiose from an anoxic stock solution prepared under 100% N2 gas and sterilized by filtration."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Adjust pH to 7.3 - 7.5. Dissolve glucose in 10 ml of distilled water and sterilize glucose separately. Aseptically add to the basis medium after sterilization."
                    }

{
                        "recipe_order": 15,
                        "step": "Prepare the medium anaerobically under 100% nitrogen. The following constituents are prepared separately and added to the autoclaved mineral salt solution: Yeast extract (20 ml of 10% w/v solution)-boiled for few minutes, not autoclaved; sucrose (20 ml of 10% w/v solution)-filter-sterilized; sulfur (10 g)-sterilized by steaming for 3 h on each of three successive days; polar lipid fraction (6 - 12ml)-prepared as described by W. Zillig et al. (1983), Syst. Appl. Microbiol. 4: 79 - 87; Na2S x 9 H2O (10 ml of 3% w/v solution)-autoclaved under nitrogen atmosphere."
                    }

{
                        "recipe_order": 16,
                        "step": "Sparge medium with 100% N2 gas mixture to make anoxic."
                    }

{
                        "recipe_order": 18,
                        "step": "after autoclaving add the following sterile solutions:"
                    }

{
                        "step": "Note: lipid fraction can be prepared from fresh or freeze-dried biomass. Cells are disrupted by autoclaving or sonication, then filter-sterilized.

Use 5 g wet or 0,2 g dried biomass in 10 ml water or buffer, and use 10ml/l of the sterile-filtered extract. Prepare under N2 conditions.

Modified from  W. Zillig et al. (1983), Syst. Appl. Microbiol. 4: 79 - 87"
                    }

{
                        "step": "Prepare the medium anaerobically under 100% nitrogen. The following constituents are prepared separately and added to the autoclaved mineral salt solution: Yeast extract (20 ml of 10% w/v solution)-boiled for a few minutes not autoclaved; sulfur (10 g)-sterilized by steaming for 3 h on each of three successive days; Na2S x 9 H2O (10 ml of 3% w/v solution)-autoclaved under nitrogen atmosphere."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Inoculate with c. 20 ml of grains of \"ginger beer plant\"."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Add tea and sucrose to a 1 l flask, pour on freshly boiled tap water and allow to stand for 15 minutes. Filter and cool to room temperature. When starting with a small amount of tea fungus use a 50 ml beaker and 10 ml of the sweetened tea (freed of leaves) which has been acidified by addition of 0.05 ml of boiled vinegar (5%). Place a small disc of a cork stopper on the surface of the tea and place the inoculum onto it. Cover the beaker with aluminium foil and incubate. (Steam the cork disc for 15 min on two successive days)."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Prepare the medium without horse serum. After autoclaving cool to 50\u00b0C, then add 100 ml/l of sterile horse serum. Transfer cultures when actively growing. Cultures die rapidly in stationary growth phase!"
                    }

{
                        "step": "Adjust pH to 7.0. For Bacillus strains the addition of 10.0 mg MnSO4 x H2O is recommended for sporulation."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Fill up with distilled water to 1000.0 ml. Adjust pH to 7.2."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Adjust pH to 7.5. Prepare the medium anaerobically under 100% N2."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Autoclave solutions of haemin (dissolved in 0.1 ml 1N NaOH, then diluted with water to 10 ml and neutralized), formate, and fumarate separately under nitrogen."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Sterilize glucose separately. Incubate in oxygen-free, 5 - 10% CO2 containing atmosphere."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Sterilize medium for 30 min at 121\u00b0C, cool to 30\u00b0C and add fresh egg mixture carefully to the medium."
                    }

{
                        "step": "* You need for 1 l of egg mixture 20 - 25 fresh eggs (not older then 1 week). Clean the eggs, wipe away with 70% alcohol, open the eggs and homogenize the egg mixture carefully."
                    }

{
                        "step": "For solid media add agar at a concentration of 12.0 g/l"
                    }

{
                        "step": "For Bacillus strains the addition of 10.0 mg MnSO4 x H2O is recommended for sporulation."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Adjust pH to 7.0 - 7.2. Rehydrate and grow lyophilized cells in liquid broth and on agar."
                    }

{
                        "recipe_order": 6,
                        "step": "Boil the medium for few minutes under nitrogen gas. Add sodium ascorbate (0.5 g) and\r\ncontinue to bubble with nitrogen gas."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Fill immediately about 10 ml medium in 15 mL hungate tubes (with rubber septum)."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Add distilled water to give a final volume of 1000 ml."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Prepare the medium anaerobically under 100% nitrogen. Sterilize thioglycolate and sulfur separately. Sterilize the sulfur by steaming for 3 h on each of three successive days."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Adjust pH to 7.0. Incubate under 5% O2 + 95% N2."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Adjust pH to 5.6. Sterilize at 121\u00b0C for 15 min."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Magnesium chloride should be sterilized separately by autoclaving, and the other ingredients should be sterilized separately by filtration."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Prepare and distribute medium anaerobically using the Hungate technique"
                    }

{
                        "step": "Dissolve and adjust pH to 7.2. Add 1.5% agar if required. Sterilize at 121\u00b0C for 20 min."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Adjust pH to 5.6. Sterilize at 121\u00b0C for 15 min."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Dissolve peptone, yeast extract and cysteine in 800 ml of distilled water. Adjust pH to 6.5 with NaOH. Add agar and dissolve by heating."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Add 2 g/l activated charcoal to the agar base solution before autoclaving. After autoclaving, cool to 45\u00b0C and add sterilized serum."
                    }

{
                        "step": "Autoclave for 15 min at 121\u00b0C. pH of the final medium is 7.5. "
                    }

{
                        "step": "Prepare and distribute medium anaerobically by using the Hungate technique."
                    }
